# ============================================================================
# AGB WHITELIST - Suricata pass rules (agent-side)
# ============================================================================
# pass rules are evaluated BEFORE alert rules, so anything matching here is
# silently allowed and never reaches the ET ruleset's alert logic. Keep this
# file tight and specific - a pass rule is a blind spot by design.
# ============================================================================

# Allow our own AGB dynamic-DNS hosts (siem/itsiem/home.agb.mywire.org,
# agbc.mywire.org) so they never generate ET DYN_DNS sid:2045987 alerts.
# Any OTHER *.mywire.org (incl. real C2 like tnt200/area51/ethdns) still
# alerts normally - this pattern only matches names starting with "agb".
pass dns any any -> any any (msg:"AGB WHITELIST: Allow AGB DDNS"; dns.query; pcre:"/agb[a-z0-9]*\.mywire\.org$/i"; sid:1000010; rev:1;)

# Add future known-good domains/IPs below, one pass rule per entry.
# Example (commented out):
# pass dns any any -> any any (msg:"AGB WHITELIST: example"; dns.query; content:"example.com"; sid:1000011; rev:1;)
